2. ENSO series, ONI (backend/data_snapshot/oni_series.parquet)
   Obtained from the NOAA Physical Sciences Laboratory. Data provided by the NOAA/OAR/PSL, Boulder, Colorado,
   USA, from their Web site at https://psl.noaa.gov/. PSL: "The information on government servers are in the
   public domain, unless specifically annotated otherwise" (https://psl.noaa.gov/disclaimer/); PSL's data are
   provided "as is" and no NOAA endorsement may be implied. PSL lists the ONI as from NOAA CPC, a three-month
   running mean of NOAA ERSST.V5 anomalies in the Nino 3.4 region.

3. Indian Ocean Dipole, DMI (backend/data_snapshot/iod_series.parquet)
   Created at NOAA PSL ("DMI HadISST1.1" in the file header), from HadISST1.1:
   HadISST data were obtained from https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/hadobs/hadisst/ and are (c) British Crown
   Copyright, Met Office, 2003 (year taken from the Rayner et al. 2003 citation; the Met Office page asks for
   the year of first publication), provided under an Open Government Licence
   (https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/2/; terms:
   https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/hadobs/hadisst/terms_and_conditions.html).
   Citation: Rayner, N. A., Parker, D. E., Horton, E. B., Folland, C. K., Alexander, L. V., Rowell, D. P.,
   Kent, E. C., Kaplan, A. (2003), Global analyses of sea surface temperature, sea ice, and night marine air
   temperature since the late nineteenth century, J. Geophys. Res. 108(D14), 4407, doi:10.1029/2002JD002670.

